 - **Refusals decided before any request:** `viola send` refuses two texts itself, before any frame: one that holds a refused character (`not-delivered  control-character`) and one whose typed text is empty once its trailing CR and LF characters are removed, the empty text included (`not-delivered  empty-text`). Each takes the same `[/ ] unable  <name>  not-delivered  <detail>` line on stderr with exit 13, and its hint as the last stderr line (for `empty-text`: `hint: the text is empty once its trailing newlines are removed; send a text with content`). Under `--json` it is one document on stdout with no stderr line. The wrapper makes the same two refusals for a frame sent straight to it.
-- **Hint line:** directly under each refusal, `hint: <one plain instruction>`, keyed by reason (or by reason · detail). Exit 21 and exit 1 each have several causes, and every cause gets its own hint, so an agent can tell the causes apart from the last stderr line (design-system cli pattern 2). The exit-1 start refusal `unable: <name> is already live` takes `hint: viola list`. `wait`, `last`, `link` and `unlink`'s exit 21 `unable  <name>  instance-unreachable` (for `link` / `unlink`, `<name>` is the driven instance) takes `hint: <name> is not running; viola list shows the live instances` when the instance is not running (`viola send`'s exit 21 keeps its `[/ ] unable` mirror with the same hint). On Linux and Windows (macOS on the recorded gap, its server check making no comparison) a frame verb (`send`, `wait`, `last`, `answer`, `pause`, `release`, `link`, `unlink`) whose server check finds that the process on the endpoint is not the recorded wrapper, or cannot make the check, writes no frame and exits 21 with the same `unable  <name>  instance-unreachable` line (`send` in its `[/ ] unable` mirror) and `hint: the process on <name>'s endpoint is not its recorded wrapper; it was not contacted` as the last stderr line; under `--json` it prints the exit-21 document `{"v":1,"error":"instance-unreachable","detail":null}` with stderr empty. There is no hint for the opaque `unknown` refusal, for `wrapper fault` or for `internal error`. A hint never quotes the sent text or any upstream text, and never names a path or a pid.
